{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/767555-2nd-edition-character-creation-gifts","id":767555,"title":"2nd edition character creation- gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-16T21:01:14-08:00","id":767555,"title":"2nd edition character creation- gifts","content":"So I've never played werewolf before. I'm looking at 2nd edition character creation, and the segment on gifts is confusing me.<br /> <br /> Okay... so there are moon gifts, shadow gifts, and wolf gifts. When you make a werewolf, he intrinsically has the first rank of his auspice's moon gift. The he gets facets of 2 shadow gifts from his auspice or tribe. Then, if he has 2 dots in his tribe's renown, he gets the second facet of their moon gift, and if he doesn't he gets a rank in a wolf gift. So overall, a starting werewolf has 4 dots in gifts. Am I reading this right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T21:07:41-08:00","id":767556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/767555-2nd-edition-character-creation-gifts#post767555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've never played werewolf before. I'm looking at 2nd edition character creation, and the segment on gifts is confusing me.<br /> <br /> Okay... so there are moon gifts, shadow gifts, and wolf gifts. When you make a werewolf, he intrinsically has the first rank of his auspice's moon gift. The he gets facets of 2 shadow gifts from his auspice or tribe. Then, if he has 2 dots in his tribe's renown, he gets the second facet of their moon gift, and if he doesn't he gets a rank in a wolf gift. So overall, a starting werewolf has 4 dots in gifts. Am I reading this right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost completely except that it's two dots in his auspice's Renown for the second Moon Gift Facet rather than his tribe's Renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T21:21:50-08:00","id":767563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/767555-2nd-edition-character-creation-gifts?p=767556#post767556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Almost completely except that it's two dots in his auspice's Renown for the second Moon Gift Facet rather than his tribe's Renown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. I tend to use them interchangeably, when they're not. That's what I meant though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T00:03:50-08:00","id":767618,"title":"","content":"So having been going through this book, I gotta say Werewolves seem really underwhelming. Like I always got the sense that the idea of them wrecking vampires like it was nothing was supposed to carry over from oWoD, but they just don't seem that impressive overall. Am I just missing the thing that makes them turn amazing and bad-ass?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T00:20:27-08:00","id":767623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/767555-2nd-edition-character-creation-gifts?p=767618#post767618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So having been going through this book, I gotta say Werewolves seem really underwhelming. Like I always got the sense that the idea of them wrecking vampires like it was nothing was supposed to carry over from oWoD, but they just don't seem that impressive overall. Am I just missing the thing that makes them turn amazing and bad-ass?</div> </div> </div> </div>You got the wrong sense, seeing as &quot;the Garou were warriors; the Uratha are hunters&quot; has been the appropriate response to this comparison since 1e.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are social predators. They're at their best working in a pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T00:42:12-08:00","id":767631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/767555-2nd-edition-character-creation-gifts?p=767618#post767618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So having been going through this book, I gotta say Werewolves seem really underwhelming. Like I always got the sense that the idea of them wrecking vampires like it was nothing was supposed to carry over from oWoD, but they just don't seem that impressive overall. Am I just missing the thing that makes them turn amazing and bad-ass?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... Gauru form heals all lethal and basing damage every turn, uses Down-and-Dirty combat to resolve all conflict with lesser opponents, and reduces all other opponents' defense. That's a power every werewolf intrinsically has. I'd say werewolves can turn amazing and badass at the drop of a hat, just with their base template abilities. Combine that with the fact that they generally hunt in packs, and not much can challenge a werewolf physically.<br /> <br /> If this is a werewolves vs. vampires thing specifically, keep in mind that a werewolf's bite is a supernatural attack in any form, and therefore isn't reduced to bashing by vampires' damage resistance. They also have pretty easy access to fire with Gift of the Elementals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T01:02:05-08:00","id":767638,"title":"","content":"An elder werewolf can potentially set everything in a ten mile radius of themselves on fire. That usually deals with the vamps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T04:51:17-08:00","id":767742,"title":"","content":"Plus they can hunt during the day without bursting into flames while vampires are stuck sleeping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T04:54:42-08:00","id":767744,"title":"","content":"Also they don't have the hard line antagonism with vampires in nWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T04:58:32-08:00","id":767747,"title":"","content":"Indeed, you can even have vampires in your pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T05:58:52-08:00","id":767775,"title":"","content":"The Barghest Facet of the Death Gifts wrecks vampires sooooooo hard... It's not even funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T08:50:16-08:00","id":767845,"title":"","content":"Oh don't get me wrong. Gauru is bad-ass, but you can only do that for a short time, and while you're doing it, you're one bad roll away from murdering everyone around you. It just seems to me that a werewolf has to go through a lot and spend quite a bit of essence to reach a level of power comparable to a vampire. I wouldn't mind so much but Werewolves are supposed to be the savage fighter types and vamps the more social splat. I'm only referencing vamps because they're the splat I'm most familiar with. I figured werewolves would have more going for them at a so-to-speak baseline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T08:57:27-08:00","id":767848,"title":"","content":"Being one bad roll away from murdering everyone around you isn't necessarily a weakness. You just need to make sure that everyone around you is a vampire. <br /> <br /> That's your problem. You're trying to have werewolves be vicious murder machines without letting them go into vicious murder machine mode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T09:11:30-08:00","id":767860,"title":"","content":"Except werewolves are pack-animals. Their nature means that there will never be a situation where everyone around them is someone they're cool with murdering. Failing that, there are still probably at least some innocent bystanders you don't want to slaughter<br /> <br /> And like I said, it's that Werewolves need to expend a lot of cost to get to where a vampire is for free. For just one example, my Rahu can spend a point of essence to add his purity of 2 to his strength for one scene. A vampire with 2 dots of vigor has those 2 dots added to his strength all the time for free, and then he can spend a point of blood to add those dots as weapon damage to his melee attacks. And then (Granted, I'm just reading the book I probably have a lot of details wrong) if the wolf wants to shift he has to spend another point of essence and then, I believe, take a turn to shift? And then bare in mind that as he's doing this, the vamp can be spending blood to match or overpower him, and the vamp can probably afford to do this because blood is a lot easier to get than essence.<br /> <br /> I'm just using this as an example. I know it's a fallacy to compare two splats just to point out how they do in a one-on-one fight. I'm just using the situation to illustrate how hard the werewolf has to work to wreak supernatural destruction, when that's the thing he's here to do. The werewolf can eventually overpower the vamp in a fight, but he's spending a lot of time and resources to get there, when I feel like it should be the vamp who has to work and spend resources to get up to his level.<br /> <br /> Gauru is Bad Ass. I just wish the werewolf could do more without having to spend essence, which seems a lot harder to refill than blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T09:26:01-08:00","id":767870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/767555-2nd-edition-character-creation-gifts?p=767845#post767845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just seems to me that a werewolf has to go through a lot and spend quite a bit of essence to reach a level of power comparable to a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Level of power comparable to a vampire for what? Are you the same poster from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage\">the other thread</a>? Because we went over this.<br /> <br /> While all vampiric disciplines require you to learn things in order, only Auspice gifts work similarly for werewolves. While gifts do cost Essence to activate, Essence is fairly easy to get, and there's a number of gift facets that activate automatically and for free when you go into death rage. Vampire abilities are also a lot more limited in what they can do, while werewolves abilities aren't just versatile, but made even moreso by fetishes, which can alter existing gifts or give you gifts you don't have.<br /> <br /> The big thing is once a werewolf goes into gauru, which they can do for a good period of time, they don't need to spend any Essence to heal and require aggravated damage which most vampires can't dole out or roll over with. Meanwhile a werewolf can cause lethal to a vampire, who's going to be needing to spend Vitae to heal, to activate their resistances, and to boost up their own powers, causing a massive drain on their Vitae.<br /> <br /> Or a werewolf can just sneak into their place during the day and rip their head off while they sleep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/767555-2nd-edition-character-creation-gifts?p=767860#post767860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except werewolves are pack-animals. Their nature means that there will never be a situation where everyone around them is someone they're cool with murdering. Failing that, there are still probably at least some innocent bystanders you don't want to slaughter</div> </div> </div> </div>If you death rage with other werewolves around, they're spurred into death rage as well, and death raging werewolves never attack each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And like I said, it's that Werewolves need to expend a lot of cost to get to where a vampire is for free. For just one example, my Rahu can spend a point of essence to add his purity of 2 to his strength for one scene. A vampire with 2 dots of vigor has those 2 dots added to his strength all the time for free, and then he can spend a point of blood to add those dots as weapon damage to his melee attacks. And then (Granted, I'm just reading the book I probably have a lot of details wrong) if the wolf wants to shift he has to spend another point of essence and then, I believe, take a turn to shift? And then bare in mind that as he's doing this, the vamp can be spending blood to match or overpower him, and the vamp can probably afford to do this because blood is a lot easier to get than essence. </div> </div> </div>You don't need to spend Essence to shift, this depends on your Harmony. At 4-6 you change reflexively for free. Lower than that and you change automatically each scene. Higher, from 7-8, you can spend Essence to change reflexively. So your werewolf is spending 1 Essence to activate their gift while your vampire is spending 1 Vitae to boost their weapon damage. But your werewolf is also changing, and presumably not going into human form so he's getting a free strength bonus, as well as free weapon damage increases. And if he's going into gauru form, he no longer needs to spend any Essence on healing. The result is that the vampire keeps spending Vitae to boost damage given, to resist damage taken, and to heal, while your werewolf has to spend 1 Essence to increase their strength on top of their already bolstered damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-17-2015, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T09:29:50-08:00","id":767875,"title":"","content":"A werewolf only needs to spend an essence and a turn to shift at the very fleshiest of harmony scores. A starting character can do it with either one or the other, and at their most balanced a werewolf can shift instantly for free at will. <br /> <br /> So in your little matchup you've got a vamp with two bonus dots of strength all the time, versus a werewolf with three bonus dots in easy reach, plus two more it can activate for a scene, plus the extra dice gained from the vampire losing his athletics contribution to defense. The vamp can add another two to their pool for a vitae apiece, but every time they do that they can't heal that turn, while the werewolf is just shrugging off everything thrown at them like it's nothing. Plus they might also have the slaughterer facet, which adds purity to natural weapon damage much like vigor can do. <br /> <br /> And here's the thing: In basu im, all that switches on for free. And yeah, there are pack members to worry about, but most werewolves know how to avoid a packmate in death rage. Or they can just join the party, because other death raging werewolves get ignored. <br /> <br /> As for essence being harder to come by than blood, well, technically no. Those &quot;human&quot; things vampires eat for sustenance are also a handy source of essence, if you're in a pinch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T09:49:29-08:00","id":767893,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=nofather;n767870]<br /> <br /> Level of power comparable to a vampire for what? Are you the same poster from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage\">the other thread</a>? Because we went over this.<br /> <br /> I am not that person. I should point out I'm not trying to whine. I'm just trying to understand the game. Part of the problem, I think, is that I know vampires really well, whereas weres are new to me and I don't know all the tricks yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T10:09:35-08:00","id":767909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/767555-2nd-edition-character-creation-gifts?p=767893#post767893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not that person. I should point out I'm not trying to whine. I'm just trying to understand the game. Part of the problem, I think, is that I know vampires really well, whereas weres are new to me and I don't know all the tricks yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. The thing is a lot of people seem to think Forsaken is supposed to be some sort of sequel to Apocalypse, when this has never been true in any fashion. Werewolves have no animosity towards vampires, nor vampires with werewolves, and in fact the two splats are probably most likely to have some sort of alliance or at least an understanding with one another since they both deal with similar issues regarding territory.<br /> <br /> But when it comes down to it unless a vampire is a werewolf hunter to begin with and optimized for it they're going to have a lot of trouble dealing with a werewolf who hunts vampires. Especially since the vampire likely won't have a pack of other hunters at their back undergoing the Sacred Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T10:10:56-08:00","id":767911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/767555-2nd-edition-character-creation-gifts?p=767875#post767875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for essence being harder to come by than blood, well, technically no. Those &quot;human&quot; things vampires eat for sustenance are also a handy source of essence, if you're in a pinch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't eating humans a super big no-no for werewolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T10:19:46-08:00","id":767921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/767555-2nd-edition-character-creation-gifts?p=767911#post767911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't eating humans a super big no-no for werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's as big a no-no as a vampire draining somebody's blood. And while the werewolf wounds will last longer (aggravated instead of lethal), the werewolf could theoretically leave the human alive. In fact, a werewolf can get a lot more Essence per turn than the vampire, since the werewolf can get up to the damage they caused with a bite (which in Gauru is at least 4) in Essence for each bite. And if they only need, say, 2 essence to top off and but dealt 6 damage, they could only get 2 Essence from the target and deal 2 Agg 4 Lethal. Much easier to deal with (the Lunacy, hospital visit, and eventual therapy will be somewhat longer-lasting issues though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T10:26:16-08:00","id":767928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/767555-2nd-edition-character-creation-gifts?p=767911#post767911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't eating humans a super big no-no for werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's part of the Oath of the Moon, but its rare for a werewolf to see all aspects of it as unbreakably sacred. Most are going to break their oaths once and awhile, some are just going to outright ignore large portions of it. Similar to the Traditions of vampires. The first is not to reveal your true nature to those 'not of the Blood.' Doing so 'forfeits you your claim to the Blood.' But nearly every vampire in existence was created by another vampire breaking that tradition, as is every ghoul.<br /> <br /> My own character has eaten seven people since we started playing. But other players have said they'd never let their characters do such a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T10:34:06-08:00","id":767932,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>A werewolf can spend an essence to shift reflexively (and then attack or whatever else he wants to), or shift for free as an instant action. Your scenario also assumes your werewolf didn't come prepared to fight in Urshul or at least Dalu.</li> <li>A werewolf in your whiteroom scenario can spend an essence to shift to Urshul and get both the benefits of 2 dots in Vigor (+2 strength for the form, +2 damage from bite attacks). He can then also initiate a grapple automatically on a successful attack. Inflict a tilt reflexively upon hitting. Has +3 health, and also does lethal damage, bypassing a vampire's natural resilience. That's the benefit of 2 dots in a discipline and more all from shifting - something any werewolf can do. He <i>could</i> then further add his Purity to his strength that same turn or later, depending on his primal urge.</li> <li>A vampire has to spend an essence a turn to match a werewolf's strength in Urshul, and 1 essence a turn to heal what takes a werewolf 1 (or free). At three primal urge a werewolf is healing 2 lethal for 1</li> <li>Death raging werewolves fight together, so that is a pack of monsters who heal all lethal damage every turn and activate combat gifts for free, use down and dirty combat for lesser enemies, grapple on successful attack, and ignore half your defense.</li> <li>All the physical disciplines have a gift equivalent (for a Rahu, at least) so they are moot with the exception of the bonus to Defense from Celerity. Werewolves can already dodge bullets in most forms, and Garou's negation of skill bonus to defense counteracts the Celerity advantage.</li> <li>If the pack has a locus, essence is incredibly easy to come by. Literally as easy as possible. A 1 dot merit gives you something like 3 essence per day and allows you to spend more essence per turn than your primal urge would allow. And really, hunting a low level spirit for essence is only slightly more difficult than hunting humans for vitae (and spirits are quite nearly as numerous).</li> <li>Your white room scenario is actually terrible for the vampire because if this werewolf is a Rahu and has the two in Purity that you've suggested, then he also can spend an essence to add 8-again to his brawl attacks for the scene, and automatically adds his Purity to his health (+2 on top of the +2 from Urshul). Both those gifts are free for the Rahu, so it puts your vampire at an incredible disadvantage. Additionally, the Rahu would have another gift, potentially scaling on Purity. Again, this is all without Garou and at equivalent experience. The vampire has its worst odds at low levels.</li> <li>The tally comes to +5 health, +2 Strength, +reflexive inflicting of a tilt, +grapple on successful hit, +bonus gift, +8-again on brawl for a grand total of 3 essence. This is what the werewolf has <i>over</i> the vampire's free addition from Vigor. The same vampire spends 2 vitae each <i>turn </i>to equal the Urshul's bite and Strength with Vigor and Physical intensity respectively. This assumes their primal urge/potency are equivalent at 1.</li> </ol>I've been whiterooming for a while now so this horse won't ever die for me. Honestly, at higher levels the vampire has a shot by overloading on physical intensity and riding the wave to try to overwhelm the werewolf before he has a chance to shift or heal it all. The werewolf does get increased healing though, so it can often just outlast the vampire's vitae. The higher you go in Potency/Urge the better the vampire's shots get. A vampire with Claw of the Unholy also can tip the scales. Until a Rahu gets Crimson Spasm then it all sort of tips right back over. At low levels though there really isn't much of a chance in a straight brawl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":".  Right, +3. Thanks Ephsy. 11-17-2015, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T13:55:17-08:00","id":768073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/767555-2nd-edition-character-creation-gifts?p=767932#post767932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>A werewolf can spend an essence to shift reflexively (and then attack or whatever else he wants to), or shift for free as an instant action. Your scenario also assumes your werewolf didn't come prepared to fight in Urshul or at least Dalu.</li> <li>A werewolf in your whiteroom scenario can spend an essence to shift to Urshul and get both the benefits of 2 dots in Vigor (+2 strength for the form, +2 damage from bite attacks). He can then also initiate a grapple automatically on a successful attack. Inflict a tilt reflexively upon hitting. Has +2 health, and also does lethal damage, bypassing a vampire's natural resilience. That's the benefit of 2 dots in a discipline and more all from shifting - something any werewolf can do. He <i>could</i> then further add his Purity to his strength that same turn or later, depending on his primal urge.</li> <li>A vampire has to spend an essence a turn to match a werewolf's strength in Urshul, and 1 essence a turn to heal what takes a werewolf 1 (or free). At three primal urge a werewolf is healing 2 lethal for 1</li> <li>Death raging werewolves fight together, so that is a pack of monsters who heal all lethal damage every turn and activate combat gifts for free, use down and dirty combat for lesser enemies, grapple on successful attack, and ignore half your defense.</li> <li>All the physical disciplines have a gift equivalent (for a Rahu, at least) so they are moot with the exception of the bonus to Defense from Celerity. Werewolves can already dodge bullets in most forms, and Garou's negation of skill bonus to defense counteracts the Celerity advantage.</li> <li>If the pack has a locus, essence is incredibly easy to come by. Literally as easy as possible. A 1 dot merit gives you something like 3 essence per day and allows you to spend more essence per turn than your primal urge would allow. And really, hunting a low level spirit for essence is only slightly more difficult than hunting humans for vitae (and spirits are quite nearly as numerous).</li> <li>Your white room scenario is actually terrible for the vampire because if this werewolf is a Rahu and has the two in Purity that you've suggested, then he also can spend an essence to add 8-again to his brawl attacks for the scene, and automatically adds his Purity to his health (+2 on top of the +2 from Urshul). Both those gifts are free for the Rahu, so it puts your vampire at an incredible disadvantage. Additionally, the Rahu would have another gift, potentially scaling on Purity. Again, this is all without Garou and at equivalent experience. The vampire has its worst odds at low levels.</li> <li>The tally comes to +4 health, +2 Strength, +reflexive inflicting of a tilt, +grapple on successful hit, +bonus gift, +8-again on brawl for a grand total of 3 essence. This is what the werewolf has <i>over</i> the vampire's free addition from Vigor. The same vampire spends 2 vitae each <i>turn </i>to equal the Urshul's bite and Strength with Vigor and Physical intensity respectively. This assumes their primal urge/potency are equivalent at 1.</li> </ol>I've been whiterooming for a while now so this horse won't ever die for me. Honestly, at higher levels the vampire has a shot by overloading on physical intensity and riding the wave to try to overwhelm the werewolf before he has a chance to shift or heal it all. The werewolf does get increased healing though, so it can often just outlast the vampire's vitae. The higher you go in Potency/Urge the better the vampire's shots get. A vampire with Claw of the Unholy also can tip the scales. At low levels though there really isn't much of a chance in a straight brawl. Until a Rahu gets Crimson Spasm then it all sort of tips right back over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Urshul gets +3 Health. +2 from Stamina, and +1 from increased Size.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}